  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">National Seed Technology Park &#x2013; Knowledge transfer project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is the second phase of the collaboration with the Philippines Department of Agriculture (DA) in establishing a National Seed Technology Park (NSTP) following the scoping mission that was conducted in November 2020.The scoping mission was commissioned to determine the needs and benefits from setting up the NSTP in support of the local seed industry.The second phase of the project is a two-year capacity-building project aimed at support of the development of an improved seed sector focusing on an effective Seed Quality system, an effective system of Plant Variety Protection, and a capacitated public-private seed production system. Training activities will, where possible, be implemented in the new to be established NSTP. These include amongst others Plant Variety Protection, variety registration, inspections, certification of improved varieties, and promotion of the access and use of high-quality seed.</narrative>
  </description>
