    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-12-31"></period-end>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project improved the regulatory and operational frameworks of the Philippine seed sector, yielding tangible benefits to the business climate. Key achievements include:
&#x2022;	Initiating Stakeholder Discussions on PVP and Laying the Foundation for a PVP Roadmap: Organizing the PVP awareness seminar was a notable accomplishment, given the sensitivity of the topic in the Philippines. The discussions brought a deeper understanding of the benefits of aligning with international standards, such as fostering innovation, enhancing international partnerships, and attracting investment. These efforts laid the groundwork for the development and implementation of the PVP roadmap, a critical step toward a more efficient and internationally compatible PVP system.
&#x2022;	Achieving ISTA Accreditation for Improved Seed Quality Certification: Through the project&#x2019;s capacity-building activities, the Philippines achieved ISTA accreditation for the BPI-NSQCS laboratory. This accreditation represents a tangible improvement in the regulatory framework, aligning local seed testing processes with international standards and fostering market expansion opportunities.
&#x2022;	Enhancing Inspection Efficiency through Protocol Development: Specific guidance and protocols were developed for seed inspectors, equipping them to conduct more accurate and efficient inspections. This directly supports a higher-quality seed supply chain, benefitting both producers and end-users.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
